    "Scouting Notes": "Has below average stuff, but his changeup is really good, he kills lift and gets some fade with heavy gyro spin.\n It misses a ton of bats and gets chases, he just has fringy feel for the pitch.\n Flashes 60, looks like a 55. \n His four seam is well below average.\n His breaker is a 45 and has slight sweep at 78 81, has added either a shorter slider or a cutter in the mid 80's that he uses a lot and is a solid pitch.",
    "Notes Updated 2": "8/3/2022",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "Has below average stuff, but his changeup is really good, he kills lift and gets some fade with heavy gyro spin.\n It misses a ton of bats and gets chases, he just has fringy feel for the pitch.\n Flashes 60, looks like a 55. \n His four seam is well below average.\n He had solid numbers this spring and got strikeouts while limiting freebies and performing despite the limited stuff in small conference. \n His breaker is a 45 and has slight sweep at 78 81, good college pitch but not gonna perform at next level without a jump in movement.",
